+# Bolt handoff — safety repair, October 4 UTC / October 3 PDT, 2026
+
+## Import this commit
+
+Sync the connected GitHub repository's `main` branch in Bolt. Run `npm ci --ignore-scripts`
+and `npm run verify`. Do not replace these files with generated timestamp files.
+
+This source repair deliberately removes unsafe automatic live entry and withdrawal paths.
+It does not claim that existing exchange holdings, historical P&L, or deployment settings are reconciled.
+
+## Deployment order
+
+1. Apply `supabase/migrations/20261004020000_secure_execution.sql` to the EXISTING project
+   using the normal migration mechanism (`supabase db push` on the correctly linked project).
+   Back up the database first. The migration preserves trade history, marks its accounting unverified,
+   pauses entries, and removes both old cron jobs by name. Do not run just the frontend and assume
+   that the old backend or public database permissions were repaired.
+2. Create the owner's password-based user in Supabase Auth (or use an existing verified owner user).
+   In the SQL editor, register that user's actual UUID; never allow self-enrollment:
+
+   ```sql
+   INSERT INTO public.app_operators(user_id)
+   VALUES ('REPLACE_WITH_OWNER_AUTH_USER_UUID'::uuid)
+   ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
+   ```
+
+   No hardcoded password, owner identity, API key, or wallet address is committed. Disable public
+   sign-ups if they are not needed; non-owners are denied even if they can create a user.
+3. Deploy all four Edge Functions, including their `_shared` imports:
+
+   ```sh
+   supabase functions deploy binance-feed
+   supabase functions deploy binance-withdraw
+   supabase functions deploy backtest-engine
+   supabase functions deploy get-config
+   ```
+
+   `verify_jwt=false` is intentional: every handler verifies the owner JWT using Auth `getUser`
+   plus the server-only owner list. Only POST `/scan` can alternatively accept the scheduler token.
+   Do not deploy any handler that omits this guard.
+4. Keep Binance.US credentials in Edge Function secrets only. Trade permission is only needed
+   for authenticated exit operations; withdrawal permission is unnecessary and should be disabled.
+   Keep the Supabase service-role key out of Vite variables and frontend bundles.
+5. Configure `VITE_SUPABASE_URL` and `VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY` in Bolt and deploy the frontend.
+   Sign in as the registered owner. Confirm anonymous API calls are rejected and authenticated
+   account/data views work. Missing configuration shows a setup message instead of a blank screen.
+6. Review all existing Binance orders and holdings. The app does not assume old trade quantities or
+   cost basis were accurate. All legacy rows start with `inventory_verified=false`, so app exits
+   are blocked until an operator compares actual exchange holdings/orders and corrects the row
+   quantities and sets that flag using backend/admin access. Manage urgent exits directly on
+   Binance.US while this verification is incomplete. The **Order recovery** panel checks newly journaled exits without placing
+   new orders. Legacy entry/cost-basis repair requires exchange history; do not set
+   `accounting_verified=true` based solely on old app P&L.
+7. Optional protective-exit scheduler: generate a random 32+ character token. Set `SCHEDULER_TOKEN`
+   in Edge Function secrets and store the same value as `app_scheduler_token` in Supabase Vault;
+   store the project URL as `app_supabase_url`. Run `supabase/setup/scheduler.sql` explicitly.
+   This creates exactly one job and never enables live entries. Check `cron.job_run_details` and
+   `net._http_response`; a successful cron invocation alone does not prove HTTP success.
+8. Reset the entry pause only after reviewing risk settings and outstanding orders. Reset does not
+   erase same-day losses and refuses unresolved order journals. New live entries remain disabled.
+
+## Semantics to preserve
+
+- **Pause / kill switch:** prevents new entries. Protective exits still run on scans.
+- **Close All:** authenticated explicit liquidation request; it pauses entries, then attempts exits.
+  Failures stay open and are shown as unresolved. It never claims every position closed merely
+  because the request completed.
+- **Recovery:** uses GET order/fill queries. No replacement order is sent after an ambiguous response.
+- **Legacy P&L:** not verified. Verified paper performance is not an exchange account balance.
+- **DeFi:** see `DEFI_RELEASE.md` for the new authenticated worker, protocol coverage and deployment prerequisites.
+
+## Remaining work before a separate live-entry release
+
+Build and validate journaled live entries, actual entry fills/commission valuation, durable account
+reconciliation and exchange-native protection; test partial fills, timeouts, process crashes, stale data,
+rate limits, balance/filter errors and third-asset fees. Reconcile existing holdings and daily account
+risk. No profit promise or live readiness follows from a passing Vite build or synthetic backtest.
