+# Live DeFi backend release
+
+This release preserves the dashboard layout. It contains real on-chain readers,
+transaction encoders, an authenticated worker, a durable execution journal and
+receipt-based token cashflow accounting. It is NOT a deployed earning strategy.
+
+## Implemented scope
+
+- Curve Ethereum: 3pool wallet LP balance and virtual price; bounded add/remove liquidity encoding.
+- Uniswap V3 Arbitrum: wallet NFT discovery and stored owed tokens; existing position increase/decrease/collect encoding.
+- Aave V3 Polygon: addresses-provider discovery, collateral/debt/health; supply/withdraw encoding.
+- Balancer V2 Optimism: vault checks and specified pool balances; weighted-pool join/exit encoding only.
+- Compound III Base: USDC market supply, debt and current variable APR; supply/withdraw encoding.
+- Every reader checks chain ID, fresh block, deployed bytecode and block-hash consistency.
+- Position coverage is explicit. Staked LP/NFT holdings and rewards are not automatically indexed.
+- Legacy dashboard profits use verified live fills; historic seed/sweep/withdrawal counters are excluded.
+- The old backtest endpoint returns 410 and scans reject paper mode. Historical test fixtures are not app simulations.
+
+## Deployment (existing project only)
+
+Project: `bydbweyercozwdxcbase`. Deployment checkpoint on October 6, 2026:
+
+- Both security migrations were applied together in a transaction through the project's SQL editor. The result confirmed `paused=true`, release `defi-2026-10-06`. They remove the legacy trading schedules and disable paper mode while retaining the kill switch. Do not rerun these migrations blindly.
+- `binance-feed` was deployed. An unauthenticated request to `/config` returned HTTP 401 with `Sign in to continue`.
+- `binance-withdraw` deployment was submitted, but completion could not be verified.
+- `get-config`, `backtest-engine`, and `defi-monitor` still need deployment. The DeFi scheduler has not been installed.
+- The database has zero Auth users; owner enrollment has not been completed.
+- Browser approval review stopped further operations because of an account usage limit. This was a review availability failure, not an unsafe-action rejection.
+- GitHub integration writes returned HTTP 403. The latest source is committed locally and packaged, but is not synced to Bolt/GitHub.
+- No wallet signer, approved capital policy, or funded transaction has been configured or executed. Complete yield reconciliation for all protocols remains outstanding.
+
+The original dashboard layout is preserved in the source. The protected backend may cause the older Bolt frontend to show access errors until owner login and the frontend update are completed.
+
+1. Record the already-applied `20261004020000_secure_execution.sql` and
+   `20261006053000_defi_control_plane.sql` in the normal deployment history after checking the database. Do not reapply them.
+2. Register the verified owner's existing Auth UUID in `app_operators`.
+3. Deploy `binance-feed`, `binance-withdraw`, `backtest-engine`, `get-config`, and
+   `defi-monitor` (its `deno.json` maps ethers). Verify anonymous requests fail.
+4. Install the frontend with `npm ci --ignore-scripts`, run `npm run verify`, then sync Bolt.
+5. Configure `SCHEDULER_TOKEN` in Edge secrets and the matching Vault secrets named
+   `app_scheduler_token` and `app_supabase_url`. Install `supabase/setup/defi-scheduler.sql`.
+   This installs one minute-based job; it does not enable spending.
+6. Insert selected wallet/protocol rows into `defi_positions` with `enabled=true`.
+   Balancer requires explicit pool IDs. Confirm heartbeat and successful RPC snapshots.
+7. Provision an independent signing-only HTTPS service using `DEFI_SIGNER_URL` and
+   `DEFI_SIGNER_TOKEN`. The service must keep keys outside the browser, enforce its own
+   exact per-job spending approvals, support durable idempotency by job UUID, and return
+   `{ "rawTransaction": "0x..." }` WITHOUT broadcasting. This repository does not provide
+   or provision that signer. Reuse of a job ID must always return the same signed bytes.
+8. Admin-provision a `defi_jobs` row with exact policy and protocol. Policy fields:
+   chain, wallet, to, data, value, maxGas, maxFeePerGas (raw decimal strings for amounts),
+   and expiresAt (Unix milliseconds). The encoder only prepares calldata; approval must
+   separately verify pool/token identity, quotes, ownership, balances, allowance,
+   expected outputs, liquidity risk and intended total spending.
+   The owner must select assets, pool/NFT IDs, limits and authorized strategy; none is guessed.
+9. Only after that provisioning and a reviewed transaction: set `DEFI_EXECUTION_ENABLED=true`,
+   unpause the worker and approve the exact job using server-side administration.
+   No browser/API route can enroll an owner, approve a job or unpause spending.
+
+## Recovery and accounting
+
+The worker serializes with existing Binance execution, stores the nonce and signed
+bytes before broadcasting, and retries only the same hash. Pending/replaced nonces,
+expired approvals, unavailable state and reorgs block new signing. Pausing stops
+broadcasts but allows receipt recovery. A submitted hash is not a settled transaction.
+Finalized canonical receipts settle the journal and ERC20 cashflows atomically.
+Signed bytes are excluded from browser SELECT privileges.
+
+Token inflows are NOT automatically profits. Compound supply interest is calculated
+only between finalized snapshots with unchanged nonnegative principal and complete
+logs showing no wallet activity. These are accrued token units, not realized USD
+income. Active intervals, other protocols' yield, gas valuation, LP cost basis,
+staked holdings, swaps and rewards require further reconciliation. No 24h/7d total
+is displayed from incomplete interval coverage. No automated capital allocation or
+cross-protocol profit strategy has been selected or enabled.
+
+## Verification
+
+`npm run verify` runs lint, both backend type checks, database/auth/execution tests,
+and production frontend build. Unit fixtures never send transactions. A release
+must additionally verify deployed RLS, owner login, cron HTTP success, real wallet
+positions and a user-approved transaction receipt. Passing tests is not evidence
+that a funded strategy is running or profitable.
