-# Bolt.new
+# Current release
 
-[![Open in Bolt](https://bolt.new/static/open-in-bolt.svg)](https://bolt.new/~/sb1-gxmkdxh3)
+See [DEFI_RELEASE.md](DEFI_RELEASE.md) for implemented protocol coverage, deployment steps and the remaining signer/accounting requirements. Deployment is not implied by source changes.
+
+# Bolt.new — trading dashboard
+
+React/Vite dashboard with Supabase Edge Functions targeting **Binance.US**.
+
+**Safety repair:** new live entries and automatic withdrawals are disabled in code.
+Paper trading is available after owner setup. Authenticated protective/emergency exits
+for inventory-verified existing live positions use exchange fills and a durable order journal. No claim of
+profitability, reconciliation of historical trades, or completed production deployment is made.
+
+Start with **[BOLT_DEPLOYMENT.md](BOLT_DEPLOYMENT.md)** when importing these changes in Bolt.
+GitHub sync updates source files; it does not apply Supabase migrations or redeploy Edge Functions.
+
+## Local verification
+
+Node 22.18+ (CI uses Node 24):
+
+```sh
+npm ci --ignore-scripts
+npm run verify
+```
+
+`verify` runs frontend lint, Edge Function type checking, offline execution regressions,
+PostgreSQL-backed migration/security tests, frontend type checking and production build.
+It does not call Binance or submit orders. Backend checking uses Deno 2.9.6 via npx.
+
+For frontend development, copy `.env.example` to `.env`, supply the project's **public**
+Supabase values, and run `npm run dev`. Keep exchange secrets only in Supabase secrets.
+
+## What is implemented
+
+- Owner session verification on every Edge Function; separate scheduler credential on POST `/scan` only.
+- Owner-scoped database reads, backend-only trade/config/journal writes.
+- One database execution lease, no automatic browser scans or duplicate cron jobs.
+- Immediate stop checks using current prices, explicit emergency close, no fabricated target-price fills.
+- Persisted client-order IDs; ambiguous/rejected responses do not close positions or trigger blind retries.
+- Owner reconciliation of existing exit orders using Binance order status and fill history.
+- Atomic, idempotent confirmed-exit application. Legacy cost basis stays unverified.
+- Paper cost model: 0.10% slippage and 0.10% commission on each side (assumptions, not account fee rates).
+
+## Explicit limits
+
+- New live entries are blocked by `LIVE_ENTRIES_ENABLED = false` and the paper-only entry function.
+  **Do not flip the constant to claim readiness.** An actual journaled live-entry pipeline, entry-fill
+  reconciliation, exchange-native protection, real account/risk reconciliation, and controlled validation
+  are still required before a separate live release. Old unsafe live-entry code has been removed.
+- Legacy positions are also marked `inventory_verified=false`; exits are blocked until actual holdings
+  and remaining quantities are reconciled by the operator.
+- Legacy live trades are marked `accounting_verified=false`. Exit fills can be verified, but historical
+  entry fees, cost basis and previously misreported closes require reconciliation with exchange history.
+- Stops run when the function is invoked; they are not exchange-native resting stop orders. Scheduler
+  outages or insufficient balance/filter failures leave positions unresolved. Review directly on Binance.US.
+- Partial/unconfirmed fills and fees in a third asset remain blocked for manual reconciliation.
+- No automatic withdrawals, bulk liquidation, or transport fallback retries are available.
+- The DeFi swarm view displays configuration only; no signer/protocol/settlement worker exists.
+- The backtest tool uses synthetic Monte Carlo paths and is not evidence of live profitability.
